#Virtual Environment
#a vritual environment is a  tool used to isolate specific pytthon environments on a single machine, allowing you to work on  multiple projects with different dependencies and packages without conflicts. 
#This can be especially useful when you are working on projects that have conflicting package versions or pacakges that are not available for a particular Python version.
#example:

#create a virtual enviornment

python-m  venv myenv #create a vitual environment
source myenv/bin/activate #activate the virtual environment on macOS and Linux 
myenv/scripts/activate #activate the enivornment for windows
to deactivate:  deactivate

